    "updated_at": "2025-12-11T15:39:27Z",
    "body": "Unless there's some kind of overarching reason I'm not aware of I don't think it's worth changing the behavior of legacy parser APIs from what is deployed.\n\nWe should think about it again though for `setHTMLUnsafe()` (if it's similarly impacted) and `setHTML()` (and streaming counterparts), but I suspect only doing \"inert\" for the \"safe\" variants is fine.",
