    "updated_at": "2025-12-11T15:42:53Z",
    "body": "> Unless there's some kind of overarching reason I'm not aware of I don't think it's worth changing the behavior of legacy parser APIs from what is deployed.\n\n\n> \n> We should think about it again though for `setHTMLUnsafe()` (if it's similarly impacted) and `setHTML()` (and streaming counterparts), but I suspect only doing \"inert\" for the \"safe\" variants is fine.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11669#issuecomment-3642166122\n\nThe inert document is needed whenever there is a sanitizer, because the sanitizer might remove images also when unsafe.\nThough we can also say that we're ok with this side effect with the unsafe+sanitizer variant.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
