    "created_at": "2025-12-11T15:56:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-11T15:57:22Z",
    "body": "> Thanks, that does seem like a compelling argument for looking into b) or possibly a) but different behavior for `setHTMLUnsafe()` and possibly some kind of toggle to configure this. Hmm.\n\nIsn't the existence of the sanitizer a good enough toggle?\nAlternatively, always use the inert document when creating elements by the parser, except for `createContextualFragment` (this only takes effect when the element is created).\n\nIn the recent blink fix for this, the inert document used for templates is reused by the sanitizer.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
